### Food Delivery Platform - Order Service
### Written for the VS Code "REST Client" extension (named requests pass ids between calls).
### Prerequisites: run restaurant-service.http and catalog-service.http first, so the owner below
### has an ACTIVE restaurant with menu items. The restaurant must be open now (opening hours).
###
### Caller identity: the access token of a sign-in below (Authorization: Bearer); its role must be
###   CUSTOMER for /cart and /orders, RESTAURANT_ADMIN for /restaurants/mine/**,
###   PLATFORM_ADMIN for /admin/**

@gateway = http://localhost:8080
# The services' shared secret of the internal APIs: the dev profile's value (INTERNAL_SERVICE_TOKEN elsewhere)
@internalServiceToken = dev-internal-service-token

@customerEmail = meera.iyer@example.com
@customerPassword = Meera1234
@ownerEmail = arjun.spicehub@example.com
@ownerPassword = Owner1234
@adminEmail = admin@fooddelivery.local
@adminPassword = ChangeMe123

# One key per checkout attempt. Re-running step 9 with the same key returns the same order.
# Change it (for example -0002) to place a new order.
@checkoutKey = checkout-demo-0001

@customerId = {{customerLogin.response.body.$.userId}}
# Every call carries the access token of a sign-in above (valid 15 minutes: sign in again after that).
@customerToken = {{customerLogin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
@addressId = {{addAddress.response.body.$.id}}
@ownerToken = {{ownerLogin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
@adminToken = {{adminLogin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
@restaurantId = {{myRestaurants.response.body.$[0].id}}
@firstItemId = {{menu.response.body.$.sections[0].items[0].id}}
@orderId = {{placeOrder.response.body.$.id}}
@onlineOrderId = {{placeOnlineOrder.response.body.$.id}}


### ============================ SETUP ============================

### 1. Register a customer (409 if it already exists: fine)
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{customerEmail}}",
  "password": "{{customerPassword}}",
  "fullName": "Meera Iyer",
  "phone": "+919845012345"
}

### 2. Customer login -> customerId
# @name customerLogin
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{customerEmail}}", "password": "{{customerPassword}}" }

### 3. Delivery address -> addressId
# @name addAddress
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/users/me/addresses
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "HOME",
  "line1": "7 Residency Road",
  "city": "Bengaluru",
  "state": "Karnataka",
  "postalCode": "560025",
  "country": "India"
}

### 4. Owner login -> ownerToken
# @name ownerLogin
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{ownerEmail}}", "password": "{{ownerPassword}}" }

### 5. The owner's restaurant -> restaurantId
# @name myRestaurants
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/restaurants/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}

### 6. The customer reads the menu -> firstItemId
# @name menu
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/restaurants/{{restaurantId}}/menu


### ============================ CART ============================

### 7. Put 2 of the first dish in the cart (live price, totals, delivery fee, tax)
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/cart/items/{{firstItemId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "quantity": 2 }

### 8. My cart
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/cart
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 8a. Optional: apply a coupon (create WELCOME100 in promotion-service.http first). The discount comes off the
###     items before tax; 422 with the reason if the cart does not qualify ("Add items worth ... more").
###     Checkout (step 9) then reserves one use of it; cancelling the order gives the use back.
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/cart/coupon
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "welcome100" }

### 8b. Remove the coupon (skip this to check out with the discount)
DELETE {{gateway}}/api/v1/cart/coupon
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}


### =========================== CHECKOUT ===========================

### 9. Place the order, cash on delivery (201, status PLACED) -> orderId
# @name placeOrder
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{checkoutKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "addressId": {{addressId}},
  "paymentMethod": "CASH_ON_DELIVERY",
  "notes": "Less spicy, please ring the bell"
}

### 10. The same request again (a network retry): 200, same order, header Idempotent-Replayed: true
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{checkoutKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "addressId": {{addressId}},
  "paymentMethod": "CASH_ON_DELIVERY",
  "notes": "Less spicy, please ring the bell"
}

### 11. Same key, different request: 422
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{checkoutKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "addressId": {{addressId}}, "paymentMethod": "CARD" }

### 12. Track the order (status + timeline)
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}


### ========================= RESTAURANT =========================

### 13. New orders waiting for a decision, oldest first
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/restaurants/mine/{{restaurantId}}/orders?status=PLACED&sort=createdAt,asc
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}

### 14. Accept
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/restaurants/mine/{{restaurantId}}/orders/{{orderId}}/accept
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}

### 15. The customer can no longer cancel (409)
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Changed my mind" }

### 16. Preparing
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/restaurants/mine/{{restaurantId}}/orders/{{orderId}}/preparing
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}

### 17. Ready for pickup: delivery-service now finds a delivery partner (see delivery-service.http)
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/restaurants/mine/{{restaurantId}}/orders/{{orderId}}/ready
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}

### 18. Today's sales
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/restaurants/mine/{{restaurantId}}/orders/sales-summary
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}

### 19. Sales for a period
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/restaurants/mine/{{restaurantId}}/orders/sales-summary?fromDate=2026-10-01&toDate=2026-10-31
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}

### 19b. Sales of one day: perHour lists its 24 hours (orders, delivered, cancelled, sales per hour)
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/restaurants/mine/{{restaurantId}}/orders/sales-summary?fromDate=2026-10-07&toDate=2026-10-07
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}


### ====================== ONLINE PAYMENT ORDER ======================

### 20. Fill the cart again
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/cart/items/{{firstItemId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "quantity": 1 }

### 21. Pay by UPI: waits for payment (PAYMENT_PENDING) until Payment Service exists (Phase 6)
# @name placeOnlineOrder
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{checkoutKey}}-upi
Content-Type: application/json

{ "addressId": {{addressId}}, "paymentMethod": "UPI" }

### 22. The restaurant does not see unpaid orders (404)
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/restaurants/mine/{{restaurantId}}/orders/{{onlineOrderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}

### 23. The customer gives up on it
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/orders/{{onlineOrderId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Payment app is not working" }

### 24. My order history
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/orders?page=0&size=20
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}


### ============================ ADMIN ============================

### 25. Admin login -> adminToken
# @name adminLogin
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{adminEmail}}", "password": "{{adminPassword}}" }

### 26. Search: one restaurant, today
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/orders?restaurantId={{restaurantId}}&fromDate=2026-10-07&toDate=2026-10-07
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 27. Search by order id
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/orders?orderId={{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 28. Order details (payment status, cancellation reason, timeline)
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/orders/{{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 29. Timeline only
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/orders/{{orderId}}/timeline
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 30. Intervention: cancel the order (audited)
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/orders/{{orderId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Customer support: rider unavailable in this area tonight" }

### 31. Audit history of the order
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/orders/{{orderId}}/audit-logs
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 32. The customer's order summary (for the admin user screen)
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/orders/customers/{{customerId}}/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### ======================= EVENTS AND SAGA (Kafka, Phases 7-10) =======================
### order-service writes its events to the transactional outbox (key = orderId):
###   OrderCreated          every checkout (payment-service keeps a copy of the order to charge)
###   OrderStatusChanged    every status the order enters (notification-service tells the customer)
###   OrderCancelled        cancelled by customer, admin or SYSTEM, or rejected by the restaurant
###                         (a PAID order is then refunded automatically by payment-service)
###   OrderPaymentRejected  a payment completed after the order was cancelled: payment-service refunds it
### It consumes PaymentStatusChanged from payment-service: SUCCESS moves a PAYMENT_PENDING order to PLACED.
### It consumes DeliveryStatusChanged from delivery-service (Phase 10): PICKED_UP moves a READY_FOR_PICKUP order
### to OUT_FOR_DELIVERY, DELIVERED to DELIVERED (a cash-on-delivery order is then PAID); ASSIGNED is a timeline note.
### Online-payment orders still unpaid after 15 minutes are cancelled by the system (ORDER_PAYMENT_TIMEOUT).
### Payment results no longer arrive over HTTP (PUT /internal/orders/{id}/payment was removed in Phase 8).
### Messages: Kafka UI http://localhost:8090

### Event schemas in Schema Registry
GET http://localhost:8091/subjects/fooddelivery.order.created-value/versions/latest

###
GET http://localhost:8091/subjects/fooddelivery.order.cancelled-value/versions/latest

###
GET http://localhost:8091/subjects/fooddelivery.payment.status-changed-value/versions/latest

###
GET http://localhost:8091/subjects/fooddelivery.delivery.status-changed-value/versions/latest

### Internal API, used by payment-service and delivery-service for orders whose OrderCreated event has not arrived yet
GET http://localhost:8084/api/v1/internal/orders/{{orderId}}
X-Service-Token: {{internalServiceToken}}

### ========================= OPERATIONS =========================

### Health (direct)
GET http://localhost:8084/actuator/health

### Swagger UI: http://localhost:8084/swagger-ui.html
GET http://localhost:8084/v3/api-docs
